1
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:03,389
In other words...

2
00:00:03,390 --> 00:00:07,560
It's possible for us to plug
that hole in Wall Maria now.

3
00:00:08,570 --> 00:00:14,200
The Scout Regiment hurry their
preparations for retaking Wall Maria.

4
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:22,710
Hell yeah! We did it, Eren!

5
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,419
Eren?

6
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,799
Let's hurry... make
weapons, and get going...

7
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:32,089
...to Shiganshina.

8
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:37,260
Seems if I inject this...
I'll turn into a Titan.

9
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:40,889
There came another...

10
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:45,520
One more thing to shape
their fate had been found.

11
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,530
Sorry I'm late.

12
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,449
Well?

13
00:00:56,450 --> 00:00:59,279
Have we discovered
what's in the container?

14
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:01,159
The thing is...

15
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:06,249
With our technology, I'm afraid
we can't dig much deeper.

16
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:08,579
Like we've heard from Eren and Historia,

17
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:13,839
it seems to originate from
some sort of human bodily fluid.

18
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:19,759
However, it vaporizes when exposed
to air, making analysis difficult.

19
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:24,849
Whoever made it must have had
technology far superior to ours.

20
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:28,769
If it was the Reiss family,
I can't imagine how...

21
00:01:28,770 --> 00:01:30,480
Hmm...

22
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:34,279
In that case, instead
of tampering with it,

23
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:37,699
we should use it to achieve
our current objective.

24
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:40,319
But who do we entrust it to?

25
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,489
Erwin, to you?

26
00:01:42,490 --> 00:01:44,329
No...

27
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:47,329
I'm no more than a wounded soldier.

28
00:01:47,330 --> 00:01:53,299
This box belongs with one of our elite
soldiers who has the best odds of survival.

29
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:56,589
Levi, would you keep it?

30
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:59,179
If it's an order, just say so.

31
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:01,550
Why even ask the question?

32
00:02:02,930 --> 00:02:07,479
We can't predict in what situation
we'll have to use this.

33
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:12,559
We'll be relying on you
to make a decision on the fly.

34
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:18,279
Judging when and who to use it on
will be for you to choose.

35
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:21,159
Can we leave that to you?

36
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:26,499
If this dream of yours comes true,
what will you do then?

37
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:29,289
I... don't know.

38
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:31,540
I won't until it happens.

39
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:35,339
I see... All right.

40
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:37,010
I'll do it.

41
00:02:41,510 --> 00:02:46,059
By the way, I'd like to unveil
that work of mine soon.

42
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:47,559
Have you given it thought?

43
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,939
You still haven't given up on that?

44
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:52,692
If the public saw that
repulsive display,

45
00:02:52,717 --> 00:02:56,689
trust in the military
would hit rock bottom.

46
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:59,490
You don't know art when you see it.

47
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:35,000
"Night of the Battle to Retake the Wall"

48
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:44,589
In other words, Eren's
father, Grisha Jaeger...

49
00:04:44,590 --> 00:04:48,849
...is likely a human who came
from outside the walls.

50
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,309
Yes.

51
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:56,729
Just like Annie, Reiner, and Bertholdt,
he possessed the Power of the Titans.

52
00:04:56,730 --> 00:05:03,029
But different from those three, he was
supportive of humanity within the walls.

53
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:06,529
If he was so interested to know
about the Scouts and such,

54
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:09,949
we could've used more
of that support of his.

55
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:11,989
I wonder...

56
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:14,329
From the moment he entered the walls,

57
00:05:14,330 --> 00:05:18,249
he was searching for the royal
family all alone, I'm sure.

58
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:19,839
And that...

59
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:24,129
That's not something you do
without incredible resolve.

60
00:05:24,130 --> 00:05:29,849
That same father wanted to show his
10-year-old son, eager to join the Scouts,

61
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:31,810
the basement of their house.

62
00:05:32,930 --> 00:05:38,229
On death's door, he said the truth
of it all was... in the basement.

63
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:41,820
What in the world do you
think is down there?

64
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:46,320
Things which mustn't be said.

65
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,239
No...

66
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:54,199
Things Grisha Jaeger couldn't say,
even if he wanted to.

67
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:58,419
That which the First Reiss King
wiped from our memories...

68
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:00,829
...memories of our world...

69
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,629
...is what I hope, but...

70
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:05,760
Pondering about it here
won't accomplish much.

71
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:10,589
The preparations finished today.

72
00:06:10,590 --> 00:06:14,769
The operation to retake
Wall Maria starts in two days.

73
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:17,349
Want to know what's in the basement?

74
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:19,939
Let's go see for ourselves.

75
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:22,980
Isn't that what Scouts do?

76
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:28,649
Let all your squads know.

77
00:06:28,650 --> 00:06:31,659
Right. Keeping it secret of course, yeah?

78
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:34,659
On a day like this,
we deserve some meat, right?

79
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:40,119
Good idea. Gotta show those kids
us adults can be counted on.

80
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:43,419
What about Commander Sadies
keeping secrets from us?

81
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:46,879
Forget about him.
We don't have time to deal with it.

82
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:50,259
I'm shocked, Hange. You used to adore him!

83
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:51,760
Shut up!

84
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,639
What is it, Levi?

85
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:00,269
It's a bit hasty, but...

86
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:03,899
What will you do after
retaking Wall Maria?

87
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:07,399
I'd guess a defense plan
comes first, but...

88
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,189
After that?

89
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:11,489
Eliminating threats.

90
00:07:11,490 --> 00:07:17,749
Outside the walls, there seems to be
someone hoping Titans will eat us all.

91
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:23,419
Of course, the answer to who
is in the basement, I imagine.

92
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:25,919
It's as I said earlier.

93
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,839
We'll plan that after the basement.

94
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:33,049
I'm asking this because you
might not live that long.

95
00:07:33,050 --> 00:07:36,350
You can't exactly move like you used to.

96
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:40,229
Let Hange call the shots.

97
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:42,849
You'll just be dead weight.

98
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:45,149
Let the good news come to you.

99
00:07:45,150 --> 00:07:48,569
We'll tell the others I
argued till you gave in.

100
00:07:48,570 --> 00:07:51,899
No... That's actually what I intend.

101
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,610
Fine with that?

102
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,870
I'm not.

103
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:07,669
I'm fine being food. Use me as bait.

104
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:10,509
The chain of command still remains.

105
00:08:10,510 --> 00:08:12,469
If I'm gone, then Hange.

106
00:08:12,470 --> 00:08:15,389
If Hange's gone, the next.

107
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:18,679
It's true, this operation
will be dangerous, but...

108
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:22,229
...to humanity, it's more
important than anything else.

109
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:24,349
That's why I've gone to such lengths.

110
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:26,859
This is all my plan.

111
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:29,649
If I don't do it, the
success rate will plummet.

112
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:33,819
That's right. The operation
might fail, but...

113
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:37,279
If you bite the dust in
the process, we're doomed.

114
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:41,369
So just sit at your desk
and keep using your head.

115
00:08:41,370 --> 00:08:44,499
That's the last thing
the Titans would want.

116
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:48,919
And for humanity,
it's the best thing going for us.

117
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:50,799
No, you're wrong.

118
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,549
Our best option is for
me to gamble it all...

119
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:56,509
Hey, hey, hey, hey! Hold up...

120
00:08:56,510 --> 00:09:01,599
Keep using that bluff around me
and I'll break both of your damn legs.

121
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:05,019
I'll make it nice and easy
to attach them later.

122
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:10,019
But the operation to retake Wall Maria
will proceed with you weeping here.

123
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:13,320
It'll be a bitch to get
to the toilet though.

124
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:17,610
I'd like to avoid that.

125
00:09:18,950 --> 00:09:21,409
What you're saying is right.

126
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:25,120
A wounded soldier should
stay off the battlefield.

127
00:09:26,250 --> 00:09:28,539
However...

128
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:31,999
There will come a moment when
we learn the truth of our world...

129
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,720
...and I must be there for it.

130
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:40,509
Is it that important to you?

131
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:42,429
More than your legs?

132
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:44,059
Yes.

133
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:47,019
More than humanity's victory?

134
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:48,350
Yes.

135
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,490
I see...

136
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:01,619
Erwin...

137
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:04,240
I'll trust your judgment.

138
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:22,599
This may be a special night, but...
let's not let the public find out!

139
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,769
Behave like soldiers
without causing a ruckus!

140
00:10:25,770 --> 00:10:28,139
Eh? Meat?

141
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:31,360
What? Is this... meat?

142
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:33,769
Am I dreaming?

143
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:37,489
Tonight's the night before
we retake Wall Maria!

144
00:10:37,490 --> 00:10:39,109
Cheers!

145
00:10:39,110 --> 00:10:40,609
Huh?! Wait!

146
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:42,949
Calm down! We'll split it evenly!

147
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:45,079
Hey! That big piece counts as two!

148
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:45,950
Hell no!

149
00:10:45,951 --> 00:10:49,709
But you suck with the spear!
You're useless, so gimme yours!

150
00:10:49,710 --> 00:10:50,789
Say what?!

151
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:53,209
Don't you start pulling
that shit, potato girl!

152
00:10:53,210 --> 00:10:55,919
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

153
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:57,379
Cut it out, Sasha!

154
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:01,089
I... I don't wanna have to kill you!

155
00:11:01,090 --> 00:11:03,550
You can't eat the whole thing alone!

156
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,679
You're eating me! Eating me! Eating me!

157
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:10,519
Sasha! That meat is Jean!
Have you lost your mind?!

158
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:13,649
Do the Scouts never get fed any meat?

159
00:11:13,650 --> 00:11:15,190
Pathetic...

160
00:11:17,610 --> 00:11:20,199
Conny, would you knock Sasha out already?

161
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,779
I'm trying!

162
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:24,829
She should be unconscious,
but she's still moving!

163
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:27,289
Hey, I think we've got casualties.

164
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:30,209
Whose brilliant idea was it to serve meat?

165
00:11:30,210 --> 00:11:33,275
Sorry. But now we know
blowing the food budget

166
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:36,234
for two months in one
night results in this.

167
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,379
That should do it.

168
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:42,800
She finally ran out of energy.

169
00:11:43,890 --> 00:11:46,219
Can you believe this freak?

170
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:49,599
And to think she once offered
to share meat with everyone.

171
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,559
Huh? When?

172
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:55,730
Four months ago, when we were
servicing the cannons.

173
00:11:57,230 --> 00:12:00,989
I brought some meat from
the officers' storehouse!

174
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:02,949
It'll be fine!

175
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:07,370
We can just raise more cattle and
sheep once we retake our land!

176
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,669
It's happening again!

177
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:17,040
The Titans are going to get in!

178
00:12:19,210 --> 00:12:20,709
It disappeared!

179
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:24,340
I thought... I felt sorry for you.

180
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:26,640
Hey.

181
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:33,939
Only four months have
passed since back then?

182
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:35,729
Only four months.

183
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:39,439
But think, in just four months,
we're in Squad Levi.

184
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,860
We climbed the ranks in a flash.

185
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,239
It's 'cuz you're a genius.

186
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,909
Damn straight I am.

187
00:12:46,910 --> 00:12:49,790
Let's eat before our food gets cold.

188
00:12:50,790 --> 00:12:52,749
Don't you see?

189
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:56,829
You're the rear guard 'cuz
you've got no experience.

190
00:12:56,830 --> 00:12:59,249
I understand that I may be weak, but...

191
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:03,259
Isn't the vanguard the best place
to learn how the enemy moves?

192
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:07,299
What's this? Trying to act all tough
talking about self-sacrifice?

193
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:12,139
But if we're all not of that mentality,
how will we be effective as a unit?

194
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:15,729
Listen here... Everyone
starts out as a recruit.

195
00:13:15,730 --> 00:13:18,424
If we throw recruits
into battle like cannon

196
00:13:18,449 --> 00:13:20,939
fodder, they'll all
be too dead to learn.

197
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:24,189
Which is why it's your job to
sit in the back and study,

198
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:27,030
so you can come home in one piece.

199
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:33,909
But the most useless of all is the suicidal
maniac who only knows how to charge in.

200
00:13:33,910 --> 00:13:35,120
Right?

201
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:40,500
Jean... Who do you mean by that?

202
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:44,169
Who else but you?

203
00:13:44,170 --> 00:13:45,839
You suicidal maniac.

204
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:48,389
Actually, I found something out recently.

205
00:13:48,390 --> 00:13:50,799
I'm quite a normal person, you know?

206
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:56,190
So if you're saying that to me,
that just makes you a coward, Jean.

207
00:13:58,270 --> 00:14:00,609
You're so full of yourself, you pig shit!

208
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:04,189
You trying to grow out the hair
on your mane, horse face?!

209
00:14:04,190 --> 00:14:05,319
Hey, what the...?

210
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,899
Just don't hit the face.

211
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:07,700
You jerk!

212
00:14:07,701 --> 00:14:09,319
You're ripping it, ass!

213
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,490
What the hell are they doing?

214
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,670
You bastard!

215
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:20,709
Show 'em what you've got!

216
00:14:20,710 --> 00:14:23,499
He's losing ground!

217
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:25,299
Looks like something started.

218
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,840
And here I told 'em to behave...

219
00:14:30,590 --> 00:14:32,009
But seriously...

220
00:14:32,010 --> 00:14:32,970
Ah?

221
00:14:32,971 --> 00:14:37,229
If you didn't have Titan powers,
you'd be dead ten times over.

222
00:14:37,230 --> 00:14:41,310
And every time, Mikasa would
swoop in to save your ass.

223
00:14:42,730 --> 00:14:45,109
If you insist on being suicidal...

224
00:14:45,110 --> 00:14:47,699
...I'll just have to kill you!

225
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:51,949
That's something I'll
have to take to heart!

226
00:14:51,950 --> 00:14:56,079
You should start showing
your mom some respect, Jean-boy!

227
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,369
Would you forget that?!

228
00:14:57,370 --> 00:14:59,000
Blargh!

229
00:15:00,330 --> 00:15:02,330
Shouldn't we stop them?

230
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:04,630
No...

231
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:08,130
I think it's fine.

232
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:15,139
Why isn't anybody stopping us?

233
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,019
How long will this go on for?

234
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:20,769
Shit... I think I'm gonna
barf up that meat.

235
00:15:20,770 --> 00:15:21,900
Hey.

236
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:27,229
You're all too damn rowdy.

237
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:29,449
Go to sleep.

238
00:15:29,450 --> 00:15:30,779
And clean that up.

239
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:32,410
Yes, sir!

240
00:15:37,490 --> 00:15:39,539
Ouch...

241
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:41,959
It's weird when I say it, but...

242
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:44,789
Shouldn't you guys watch out for me more?

243
00:15:44,790 --> 00:15:49,340
I knew if you got hurt it would
heal up quick, so I just watched.

244
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:52,839
That's so cruel.

245
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:55,469
You're the one who incited it.

246
00:15:55,470 --> 00:15:58,560
But... at least you're spunky again.

247
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:05,269
I'm glad we met the commandant.

248
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:08,189
I... It doesn't...

249
00:16:08,190 --> 00:16:13,069
Whether I'm spunky or not,
I'll do what I have to do.

250
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:15,199
But, yeah...

251
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,159
It's easier now.

252
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:20,620
Kept thinking about stuff I can't change.

253
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:27,419
And wondering why I can't be
strong like Mikasa and Levi...

254
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,250
I was jealous.

255
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:36,389
But even you and the captain...
alone, you can't do much.

256
00:16:36,390 --> 00:16:41,099
Which is why we've all gotta
find the things we can do.

257
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:45,850
And by joining together,
that's what makes us powerful.

258
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,779
Every person is different.

259
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,360
And it's all for times like this.

260
00:17:01,910 --> 00:17:03,330
Yeah...

261
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:06,380
I think you're right.

262
00:17:25,850 --> 00:17:28,359
Once we retake Wall Maria...

263
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:31,859
...and defeat all the
enemies coming for us...

264
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:34,489
...will they come back?

265
00:17:34,490 --> 00:17:37,109
Those days...

266
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:39,199
We'll bring it back.

267
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:43,159
But some things are forever changed.

268
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:45,870
We'll make them pay for that.

269
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:49,339
Yeah.

270
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,590
But there's more than that.

271
00:17:53,050 --> 00:17:55,049
The sea...

272
00:17:55,050 --> 00:17:58,549
A salt lake so big that merchants
could spend their whole lives

273
00:17:58,550 --> 00:18:01,220
and still not get all the salt.

274
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:06,439
There's more than just
Titans outside the walls.

275
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:11,649
Fiery water, lands of
ice, sandy snowfields...

276
00:18:11,650 --> 00:18:16,279
I joined the Scouts so
I could see all that.

277
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:20,240
Y-Yeah. You sure did.

278
00:18:28,250 --> 00:18:29,669
Right?!

279
00:18:29,670 --> 00:18:31,999
Let's start by seeing the sea!

280
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,549
You still doubt that it's real, Eren!

281
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:37,799
You'll see! It does exist!

282
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:39,469
All right then.

283
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:41,679
Guess we'll have to go see.

284
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,309
It's a promise, then!

285
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:44,519
You have to!

286
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:47,559
...Yet another conversation only you two
get... We can explore the outside world!

287
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:51,059
It's gotta be way bigger
than inside the walls!

288
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:53,070
Okay, I get it.

289
00:19:00,030 --> 00:19:02,070
Just before sunset...

290
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:05,620
It's finally time.

291
00:19:17,630 --> 00:19:20,219
Hey!

292
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:22,509
Hange!

293
00:19:22,510 --> 00:19:23,759
Good luck!

294
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:25,849
Flegel?

295
00:19:25,850 --> 00:19:29,689
Take back Wall Maria for us!

296
00:19:29,690 --> 00:19:33,479
The future of humanity is in your hands!

297
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,519
Captain Levi!

298
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:39,699
Thank you for saving our city!

299
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:43,659
You all come back in
one piece, all right?!

300
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:47,869
But go and reclaim our territory!

301
00:19:47,870 --> 00:19:50,289
Someone's got a big mouth.

302
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:53,749
Well, with the commotion we made,
of course they'd find out.

303
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:58,049
The thing is, all that meat we ordered
was from the Reeves Company.

304
00:19:58,050 --> 00:19:59,719
Damn that Flegel.

305
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:03,719
...Yeah! You can count on us!
...You know we will!

306
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:07,929
How long's it been since the Scouts
got a send-off like this?

307
00:20:07,930 --> 00:20:12,349
Who knows? I don't think we've ever...

308
00:20:12,350 --> 00:20:16,150
As far as I'm aware, this is a first.

309
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,879
The final operation to
retake Wall Maria...

310
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,670
...will now commence!

311
00:20:44,550 --> 00:20:48,760
Advance!

312
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,510
You guys...

313
00:22:45,630 --> 00:22:48,719
Do you have the faintest damn clue...

314
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,679
...what you're doing?!
